# Everything in this repo is consumed by a Linux AOSP build, and several files
# are parsed by C that splits on '\n' and compares the rest byte-for-byte. A
# CRLF checkout does not fail loudly anywhere — it fails as "the feature quietly
# does nothing":
#
#   prebuilt/hosts        _gethtent() (getaddrinfo.cpp) NUL-terminates at the
#                         '\n' and strcasecmp's the hostname token, so a
#                         trailing '\r' kills all 2,000 entries at once and the
#                         file still looks perfectly plausible.
#   prebuilt/*.txt        nr_parse_line() trims bytes <= ' ', so these survive a
#                         CRLF checkout — but they feed gen_l0_hosts.py's
#                         exclusion sets, and a mismatch there re-opens the
#                         never-block floor rather than reporting anything.
#   rom/*.patch           `git apply` rejects a patch whose context lines gained
#                         a '\r'; this one at least fails loudly.
#   rom/sepolicy/*, *.rc  read by the build and by init.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's default core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites the working tree on checkout. Pin it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated artefacts that must never be touched by any filter.
prebuilt/baseline.domains.xz  binary
*.png                         binary
*.jpg                         binary
*.webp                        binary
*.so                          binary
*.jar                         binary
*.keystore                    binary
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
